"SQ-01","1","Survive the promised fire fragment, then determine what the burned ravine and active portal are.","Open on direct rescue action, cut before the outcome, inspect persistent block evidence and enter when no ordinary destination explains it.","Burning cabin fragment, ruined west rim and north-wall portal cave","The region is unvisited, the cabin is deliberately built, the frame is active and no owner or body exists.","The portal leads to the same pristine ravine before any player construction.","The protagonist crosses by choice and loses his temporal and geographic certainty.","An environmental mystery becomes one-way displacement.","180","Keep the cold open under forty seconds; show no silhouette, written message or second avatar."
"SQ-02","2","Establish a safe life while preserving access to the absent portal site.","Camp on the west shelf, obtain bones through survival play, tame Moss and expand the shelter through repeatable routines.","Pristine ravine, west shelf cabin and nearby spruce terrain","Night pressure, limited supplies and the absent frame make immediate return impossible.","The efficient cabin footprint begins matching the ruin seen before entry.","The protagonist gains a home and companion but also creates emotionally costly future evidence.","Stranded survival becomes attachment in borrowed time.","260","Prioritise real taming, following, feeding, building and sit-release gameplay over montage abstraction."
"SQ-03","3","Prevent the remembered ruin and leave with Moss safely.","Match construction details, stone-clad the timber route, pack for departure and neutralise the lava shelf before dawn.","Cabin, ravine stair and lava shelf","The portal may require obsidian, night makes immediate travel unsafe and one timber support remains hidden behind the cladding.","Mining the cooled hazard opens a lateral lava source to the concealed support.","The protagonist acts on foreknowledge, but the prevention operation becomes the fire’s physical cause.","Hopeful control becomes urgent consequence.","250","Make every matched clue readable in block placement; the fire path remains provisional until tested."
"SQ-04","4","Reach and release Moss before the fire consumes the sitting place.","Ignore storage and structural defence, route the single water source towards Moss and break the shortest wall path.","Burning stair, cabin main room and bedside sitting place","Fire has entered separated blocks, Moss remains seated and the protagonist begins below the cabin.","He arrives within interaction range only after the terminal damage interval.","Moss dies and the burned shell becomes the ruin from the opening.","Immediate care becomes grief and full causal recognition.","300","The wolf must never appear penned; test the timing and stage the death without invented keepsakes or false mechanical claims."
"SQ-05","5","Reconstruct and activate the temporal frame before grief gives way to acceptance.","Trace the burn, use mined obsidian, copy the remembered frame and improvise a lava-and-spruce ignition.","Burned cabin route and north-wall portal cave","The safe ignition tools are lost, the protagonist is damaged, rescue water removed a branch torch and a creeper can approach from darkness.","The creeper kills him, but its blast releases lava to the remaining spruce and allows fire to activate the frame.","The builder mystery, blast scar and active opening portal receive one tragic causal answer.","Failed return becomes the threshold that began the journey.","210","No simultaneous double is needed; verify the blast, lava, fire, portal and item-destruction chain before lock."
