"SC-01","SQ-01","Burning west-rim cabin and shared sleeping area","World W3 at night; personal order 5; presented first as a cold open","Close protagonist","Promise immediate danger, establish that Moss outranks the structure and withhold only the rescue outcome.","The cabin is already burning and the protagonist is below Moss’s sitting place.","Reach and release Moss.","The relationship is the human stake and the opening must not imply a choice between life and property.","Separated fire blocks cut the route while the wolf remains seated.","Fire geometry and elapsed time.","Ignore storage, empty water towards Moss and break the shortest wall route.","The protagonist spends no action defending possessions once Moss is threatened.","The fire’s cause, portal connection and Moss’s fate remain unknown.","Panic to concentrated care, then interruption.","Water passes a burning chest as Moss appears through flame.","His hand reaches interaction distance and the film cuts.","The rescue remains unresolved but morally unambiguous.","What caused the fire, and did he reach Moss in time?","SP-05;SP-07","Hook, promise and emotional orientation.","Short reproducible fire stage, seated wolf line of sight, real water and breaking actions, and no claim that the outcome has been production-tested."
"SC-02","SQ-01","Ruined west-rim cabin and ravine overlook","World W5 near dusk; personal order 1","Close protagonist","Introduce the environmental authorship mystery without suggesting a visible intruder.","The protagonist is on a solo expedition at the unexplored edge of his map.","Cross the ravine before night and understand whether the ruin offers shelter.","Its construction should not exist in a region he has never visited.","The wooden upper cabin is gone, but player-made stone geometry and a descending stair remain.","Persistent aftermath, fading light and the protagonist’s own knowledge of the save.","Check map context, read the foundation, inspect the protected chest recess and follow the stair.","The ruin was built efficiently around the same natural granite seam and stone rib.","It is his later work, Moss lived here and the portal waits below.","Ordinary caution to unsettled recognition without an answer.","A repeated overlook frames the L-shaped foundation and purple light under the ravine lip.","The portal hum supplies a live route beneath a dead structure.","He descends rather than camping in the ruin.","Why is an active portal connected to a cabin with no history?","SP-01;SP-06","Grounds mystery in Minecraft construction and spatial persistence.","Burned cabin state, map-edge or coordinate context, reusable overlook, no body, no sign and no silhouette."
"SC-03","SQ-01","North-wall portal cave","World W5 at dusk; personal order 1","Close protagonist","Pose the title question through block evidence and make entry an accountable decision.","He expects the stair to lead to the ruin’s mine or cellar.","Explain the active frame before choosing whether to cross.","The portal is the only surviving system that may account for the impossible construction.","A blast cavity, exposed lava, cobblestone foot and plank remnant show recent causality but no builder.","The active frame and uncertain destination.","Inspect block faces, lava access, dark branch, frame economy and absence of recoverable drops.","The portal was physically constructed and activated near a recent explosion.","The protagonist built it after Moss’s death; fire rather than the explosion directly activated it.","Unease to chosen risk.","His hand rests on the water-cooled foot before moving into the portal plane.","He enters when observation alone cannot answer the contradiction.","The known world gives way to temporal displacement.","Where and when does this portal lead?","SP-02;SP-03;SP-09;SP-10;SP-11;SP-12","Inciting agency and a dense but fair clue cluster.","Exact portal hero set, blast cavity, lava and plank continuity, controlled transition, and no unsupported explosion-to-fire implication."
"SC-04","SQ-02","Bare north-wall cave and pristine ravine","World W0 several days before W5; personal order 2","Close protagonist","Prove earlier time through missing construction and repeated natural geography.","He expects a Nether arrival or another built exit.","Determine location, time state and immediate survival options.","Without orientation he cannot choose whether to wait, travel or reconstruct a route.","The portal plane collapses to bare stone, evening approaches and the distant established base is unreachable before night.","Temporal displacement, terrain and daylight.","Match the granite seam, stone rib, lava shelf and tree line; then secure the only flat ledge.","This is the same ravine before every player-placed block from the opening.","The exact interval, portal builder and future relationship remain unknown.","Disorientation to practical resolve.","The opening portal outline becomes bare rock in the same camera position.","He chooses a temporary camp beside the evidence instead of a blind night journey.","Stranded investigation becomes survival.","What will he build in the place whose ruin he already saw?","PAY-02;SP-01","Establishes the temporal rule through environment.","Pristine saved state, matched camera positions, day-night pressure and no second-avatar capture."
"SC-05","SQ-02","West-rim shelter, spruce terrain and cabin interior","World W0 through W1 across several in-game days; personal order 3","Close protagonist and Moss","Create an earned relationship and turn a temporary camp into the future home.","The protagonist is alone, provisionally sheltered and still seeking a return route.","Survive, tame Moss and establish a workable daily routine.","The later loss needs lived attachment, and every future structure needs an ordinary origin.","A skeleton, limited bones, building work, routine damage and the lava hazard complicate progress.","Night mobs, resource scarcity and ordinary animal behaviour.","Defeat the skeleton, attempt taming, feed Moss, gather spruce, build around the wolf and use sit only before ravine mining.","Moss enters the story through normal play; the bedside wait and release-on-return pattern becomes habitual.","The routine will make self-evacuation impossible during the fire.","Wariness to humour, trust and ease.","Moss occupies a planned stair block, follows a timber run and later waits beside the bed until released.","The protagonist stops calling the cabin temporary.","A stranded interval becomes a shared home.","Why do parts of this new home feel familiar?","SP-04;PAY-01","Relationship, normality, geography and mechanical setup.","Real skeleton drop, taming attempts, feeding, follow and sit states, staged construction progress and no pen or doghouse."
"SC-06","SQ-03","Cabin foundation, stone chest recess and ravine overlook","World W2 in daylight; personal order 4","Close protagonist","Convert repeated environmental detail into recognition of the cabin’s future.","He believes resemblance to the opening ruin may be incidental.","Compare the finished build against remembered landmarks.","If the ruin is this home, Moss is already inside a known danger pattern.","Fire removed the opening cabin’s upper form, so proof depends on surviving stone geometry rather than exact decoration.","Persistent blocks and the protagonist’s reluctance to accept the implication.","Align the granite notch, L-shaped footing, chest recess and stair rib from the opening viewpoint.","He has built the cabin whose burned remains preceded the portal.","The exact fire source, Moss’s fate and whether departure can avoid it remain unknown.","Unease to dread, then active determination.","A matched camera move turns the intact foundation into the remembered ruin without showing another person.","He packs to leave with Moss at dawn and identifies lava as the most credible hazard.","Mystery becomes a prevention problem.","Can practical changes stop the remembered fire?","PAY-01;SP-06","Major recontextualisation through construction rather than exposition.","Coordinate-accurate foundation, granite, recess and stair matches with reversible intact and ruined states."
"SC-07","SQ-03","Cabin, ravine stair and lava-shelf approach","World W2 at dusk; personal order 4","Close protagonist and Moss","Give the protagonist a sensible prevention strategy and prepare the hidden flaw.","He knows the cabin burns and intends to leave with Moss.","Make the cabin safe for one final night, neutralise the lava and depart at dawn.","Immediate night travel is dangerous, but waiting without changing the fire route would be passive.","One stripped-spruce support remains behind the new stone cladding, and the return mechanism may require obsidian.","Terrain, night pressure and incomplete visual access.","Pack supplies, replace exposed timber with stone, keep one water source ready and inspect the lava shelf.","He prioritises departure with Moss and does not plan to defend the cabin as property.","The cladding conceals a continuous flammable route and mining will expose lateral lava.","Fear to practical hope.","Packed bundles sit beside the door while stone covers the visible stair and one log seam disappears behind it.","He seats Moss beside the bed and descends for the final operation.","Is the apparent firebreak actually complete?","SP-04;SP-06;SP-07","Agency, credible risk management and causal preparation.","Readable shared sleeping area, packed-departure props, stone-cladding build, concealed-support cross-section and complete production blocking."
