ng above it as home.\",\"CE-01|CE-09\",\"parallel_cause\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"In the revealed earlier moment, mark the new place and stay with Moss.\",\"The earlier protagonist opens his blank journal, records the ravine and chooses to investigate the hum below.\",\"The apparent beginning is identified as the final portal's receiving reality and the first decision leads towards the same journey.\",\"Linear presentation closes into a cross-reality loop.\",\"The R4 frame projects the R0 portal, the blank journal precedes the Atlas and the pair are about to find the threshold.\",\"Tragic death gives way to tenderness, recognition and inevitable continuation.\",\"\",\"pass\",\"Without the vertical reveal and repeated decision, the portal destination, journal image and requested loop remain incomplete.\",\"Use an omniscient through-ground transition, the exact SC-02 surface composition and repeated audio rather than implying player survival.\"", ".studio/internal/story/sequence-outline.csv": "sequence_id,order,temporary_goal,strategy,primary_location,complications,reversal,outcome,story_state_afterward,estimated_seconds,production_note\n\"SQ-01\",\"1\",\"Survive the promised fire image, then understand the clearing and impossible portal beneath it.\",\"Open on direct rescue action, cut before the room reveal, return to the pair's arrival and let map evidence and portal hum pull them into the ravine.\",\"R4 burning house fragment, R0 clearing and R0 ravine cave\",\"The cold open supplies unexplained loss while the unvisited R0 frame contradicts the protagonist's authorship knowledge.\",\"The crying portal leads to the same ravine in a different reality.\",\"The protagonist and Moss cross by choice and lose their original context.\",\"A proposed home becomes a cross-reality mystery.\",\"160\",\"Reserve the exact clearing image for SQ-05 and show no local builder, message or second avatar.\"\n\"SQ-02\",\"2\",\"Get back to R0 and determine how the crying portal selects destinations.\",\"Explore the first echo, attempt a return, mark successive mouths, compare coordinates and use the Weeping Atlas only after observed evidence supports it.\",\"R1 Rain Echo, R2 Ash Echo, R3 Archive Echo and R4 dead mouth\",\"Each apparent return advances the chain, local marks disappear, supplies diminish and the Archive mouth destabilises.\",\"The Atlas offers a keyed return method, but the final uncontrolled crossing strands them in R4 without the necessary materials.\",\"Confusion becomes a reliable model and a long-term problem.\",\"Knowledge replaces panic, but knowledge cannot provide immediate escape.\",\"310\",\"Give every echo one strong state change and one informational function; keep Atlas inserts concise.\"\n\"SQ-03\",\"3\",\"Make R4 habitable while preparing a survivable first-threshold route.\",\"Stay beside the ravine seam, build a compact home, establish Moss's rug routine and acquire crying obsidian and glowstone gradually.\",\"R4 clearing, house, ravine and conventional supply route\",\"The local mouth is inert, the full frame is resource-intensive and the open hearth appears safely surrounded by stone.\",\"The final supply journey leaves Moss sitting beside wool within the fire-spread range.\",\"Stranding becomes home while the return plan creates the conditions for absence.\",\"Patient coexistence becomes latent domestic danger.\",\"265\",\"Use lived construction and survival actions; the fireplace-to-wool geometry remains provisional until tested.\"\n\"SQ-04\",\"4\",\"Return through the burning house, find Moss and determine whether any present-world action remains.\",\"Ignore supplies, direct water and block breaking towards the shared room, search the ruin and nearby terrain, then trace the burn fan to the rug.\",\"R4 burning house, burned clearing and ravine entrance\",\"Moss's sit state, progressed fire and lack of recoverable evidence deny a clear rescue or answer.\",\"Moss is gone, and the materials just brought home make the Atl