d the meaning of the materials remain unknown.\",\"Shock to concentrated rescue, then interruption.\",\"Water crosses the burning rug as the protagonist reaches through smoke.\",\"The image cuts before the room is visible.\",\"The rescue remains unresolved but its priority is clear.\",\"What happened while he was away, and is Moss still inside?\",\"SP-11\",\"Hook, emotional orientation and material mystery.\",\"Controlled partial fire state, dropped crying materials, real movement and water blocking, exact continuation reserved for SC-10, and no claim of mechanical validation.\"\n\"SC-02\",\"SQ-01\",\"R0 clearing and ravine overlook\",\"R0 morning; personal order 1 after the cold open\",\"Close protagonist and Moss\",\"Establish the pair, blank survey journal and surface composition later revealed as the portal destination.\",\"The protagonist and Moss have reached an unvisited but resource-rich clearing.\",\"Decide whether to stop and establish a base.\",\"The choice defines home before the portal makes location unstable.\",\"The ravine is remote, but it offers water, stone, timber and a natural overlook.\",\"Terrain, distance and ordinary survival needs.\",\"Check the map, draw the ravine symbol, let Moss settle and place a temporary marker.\",\"Moss and the protagonist are already a functioning pair and voluntarily choose the place.\",\"An active crying portal waits below and the scene is the far end of the final connection.\",\"Travel weariness to quiet belonging.\",\"Moss sits at the ledge while the clean journal opens on the first ravine sketch.\",\"A low hum from below changes settlement into investigation.\",\"They descend together rather than beginning construction immediately.\",\"What could be active beneath an untouched clearing?\",\"SP-01;SP-03;SP-12\",\"Relationship foundation, audience orientation and final-image setup.\",\"Exact repeatable morning wide shot, controlled wolf position, clean journal insert, ravine marker and a recorded audio layer reus