t.\",\"He surrounds the flame with stone but places a wool rug inside its potential spread range.\",\"CE-05\",\"Make the home, Moss routine and fire cause one continuous visual choice.\",\"The cold-open house and rug arise from care rather than decorative coincidence.\",\"Moss settles on fresh wool while the stone hearth burns behind it.\",\"Building rhythm, feeding and domestic fire replace heavy narration.\",\"120\",\"SC-08\"\n\"BEAT-09\",\"SQ-03\",\"9\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Prepare the first-threshold method without risking an incomplete activation.\",\"A full crying frame and charged anchor require more materials than he has.\",\"He gathers gradually, studies the torn blast page and plans one final supply run.\",\"CE-06\",\"Give the final inventory an ordinary origin and contrast patience with later haste.\",\"He understands that activation is dangerous before Moss disappears.\",\"Crying blocks, glowstone slots and a rough stone-baffle sketch accumulate beside the Atlas.\",\"Measured inventory sounds support restrained explanation.\",\"85\",\"SC-08\"\n\"BEAT-10\",\"SQ-03\",\"10\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Collect the remaining crying obsidian and glowstone without exposing Moss to the dangerous route.\",\"The open hearth is left burning and Moss's familiar safe command position is the wool rug.\",\"He seats Moss, leaves through the conventional supply route and returns carrying the final materials.\",\"CE-06\",\"Join the portal plan, absence and fire setup through one responsible-looking decision.\",\"The exact conditions of the cold open are now in place.\",\"The door closes on Moss beside the hearth; the shot holds after the protagonist leaves.\",\"Footsteps fade until only the fire remains.\",\"60\",\"SC-09\"\n\"BEAT-11\",\"SQ-04\",\"11\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Reach Moss immediately after seeing smoke on the return ridge.\",\"Fire has spread from the rug into timber and obscured the shared room.\",\"He completes the cold-open route, reaches the sitting place and finds it empty.\",\"CE-07\",\"Resolve the opening action without creating a property-versus-life choice.\",\"Moss is gone in R4, though no body or death message establishes the exact fate.\",\"The camera continues past the earlier cut to the consumed rug position.\",\"Narration falls silent through the search of the room.\",\"125\",\"SC-10\"\n\"BEAT-12\",\"SQ-04\",\"12\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Search beyond the house and decide what the remaining evidence allows.\",\"There is no response nearby, while the burn fan leads back to the rug and the Atlas promises only a dangerous route.\",\"He retrieves the dropped materials and carries the Atlas into the ravine.\",\"CE-08\",\"Let grief become a consequential decision after a credible search.\",\"The final supply run caused his absence, but it also completed the inventory needed to reach the first threshold.\",\"Empty paths give way to crying blocks stacked at the dead mouth.\",\"Sparse narration states belief rather than certainty about Moss.\",\"70\",\"SC-10\"\n\"BEAT-13\",\"SQ-05\",\"13\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Build the exact full crying frame and a survivable activation position.\",\"The Atlas requires direct discharge and its final blast-distance measurement is torn away.\",\"He completes the frame, charges the anchor and accepts an incomplete stone baffle.\",\"CE-09\",\"Pay off builder identity, materials and the knowledge source before the climax.\",\"The portal nobody made in R0 is materially constructed by the protagonist in R4.\",\"Opening portal close-ups recur as each crying block takes its coordinate.\",\"Placement sounds echo the initial inspection in reverse order.\",\"90\",\"SC-11\"\n\"BEAT-14\",\"SQ-05\",\"14\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"Wake the frame and cross to the first threshold.\",\"Direct interaction keeps him inside the unverified blast problem.\",\"The anchor explodes and kills him; after the debris settles, the invented portal field lights.\",\"CE-09\",\"Resolve the final choice through mechanism rather than exposition.\",\"The activation succeeds after its intended traveller is dead.\",\"White blast, still frame, then purple light through smoke.\",\"The explosion cuts all sound before the portal hum slowly returns.\",\"55\",\"SC-12\"\n\"BEAT-15\",\"SQ-05\",\"15\",\"PROTAGONIST\",\"In the revealed R0 moment, choose whether the clearing should become home.\",\"Neither the earlier protagonist nor Moss knows the active receiving mouth waits beneath them.\",\"The camera rises into the repeated arrival, the blank journal opens and the decision to stay leads towards discovery.\",\"CE-10\",\"Close the spatial, journal and emotional loop in one visual transformation.\",\"The final portal reaches the Return to the beginning reality and precedes its own discovery.\",\"Stone becomes soil, then the exact morning wide shot of Moss at the overlook.\",\"The opening line repeats as a faint portal hum enters below it.\",\"65\",\"SC-13\""},{"path":".studio/internal/story/scene-cards.csv","content":"scene_id,sequence_id,location,time,pov,scene_purpose,entry_state,objective,reason_objective_matters,obstacle,opposing_agent,tactics,information_revealed,information_withheld,emotional_progression,visual_event,turn,outcome,exit_state,new_question,setup_or_payoff,story_value,production_requirements\n\"SC-01\",\"SQ-01\",\"R4 burning house and shared main room\",\"R4 at night; late personal order; presented first as a cold open\",\"Close protagonist\",\"Promise urgent relationship loss and establish that Moss outranks possessions.\",\"The protagonist returns over the ridge carrying portal materials and sees the house already burning.\",\"Reach Moss through the shortest available route.\",\"Moss is the shared-life stake and the opening cannot imply that the protagonist pauses to save property.\",\"The wool rug and timber interior are burning while Moss is not visible from outside.\",\"Fire geometry and elapsed absence.\",\"Drop crying obsidian and glowstone, place water towards the room and break the shortest wall.\",\"The protagonist spends no action on storage and has returned with unexplained portal materials.\",\"The fire's cause, Moss's location and the meaning of the materials remain unknown.\",\"Shock to concentrated rescue, then interruption.\",\"Water crosses the burning rug as the protagonist reaches through smoke.\",\"The image cuts before the room is visible.\",\"The rescue remains unresolved but its priority is clear.\",\"What happened while he was away, and is Moss still inside?\",\"SP-11\",\"Hook, emotional orientation and material mystery.\",\"Set and state: R4 house in a controlled partial-fire condition. Props and mechanics: dropped crying obsidian, glowstone, water placement and a breakable rescue wall. Continuity and capture: exact action and camera match for SC-10; no mechanical validation is claimed.\"\n\"SC-02\",\"SQ-01\",\"R0 clearing and ravine overlook\",\"R0 morning; personal order 1 after the cold open\",\"Close protagonist and Moss\",\"Establish the pair, blank survey journal and surface composition later revealed as the portal destination.\",\"The protagonist and Moss have reached an unvisited but resource-rich clearing.\",\"Decide whether to stop and establish a base.\",\"The choice defines home before the portal makes location unstable.\",\"The ravine is remote, but it offers water, stone, timber and a natural overlook.\",\"Terrain, distance and ordinary survival needs.\",\"Check the map, draw the ravine symbol, let Moss settle and place a temporary marker.\",\"Moss and the protagonist are already a functioning pair and voluntarily choose the place.\",\"An active crying portal waits below and the scene is the far end of the final connection.\",\"Travel weariness to quiet belonging.\",\"Moss sits at the ledge while the clean journal opens on the first ravine sketch.\",\"A low hum from below changes settlement into investigation.\",\"They descend together rather than beginning construction immediately.\",\"What could be active beneath an untouched clearing?\",\"SP-01;SP-03;SP-12\",\"Relationship foundation, audience orientation and final-image setup.\",\"Set and capture: repeatable R0 morning clearing, ravine overlook and locked wide-shot position. Performance and props: controlled Moss mark, clean journal insert, ravine symbol and temporary marker. Continuity: preserve lighting, blocking and audio references for SC-13.\"\n\"SC-03\",\"SQ-01\",\"R0 north-wall ravine cave\",\"R0 later that morning; personal order 1\",\"Close protagonist and Moss\",\"Pose the title question and make the first entry an accountable decision.\",\"The pair follow the hum into a cave with no player route or mine.\",\"Explain enough of the active frame to decide whether to cross.\",\"The frame is the only evidence capable of challenging the protagonist's private-world knowledge.\",\"A complete crying-obsidian portal should not behave like a normal Nether frame and has no local construction evidence.\",\"The impossible active threshold and uncertain destination.\",\"Inspect coordinates, frame faces, surrounding natural blocks and absence of dropped or written evidence; keep Moss close before crossing.\",\"The portal is deliberate in shape but has no local builder or approach history.\",\"It is the receiving mouth of the protagonist's final R4 construction.\",\"Curiosity to unease, then chosen risk.\",\"The protagonist's hand and Moss's silhouette enter the purple plane together.\",\"He chooses action when inspection reaches its limit.\",\"Both leave R0 through the impossible frame.\",\"Does it lead to the Nether, another location or another version of this place?\",\"SP-02;SP-05\",\"Inciting agency and title mystery.\",\"Set and effects: complete active crying-obsidian hero frame in an untouched natural cave, with a transition language distinct from a vanilla Nether portal. Blocking and continuity: safe repeatable player-and-wolf entry, coordinate insert and matching frame geometry for SC-11.\"\n\"SC-04\",\"SQ-02\",\"R1 Rain Echo